From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: apple: Accept the A8X GXA6850 core revision

The A8X (T7001) GPU is a GXA6850 (G4G). With DWI held on, its
CORE_REVISION reads 0x00070500, as on iPadOS (measured on a J81). The
A8 (GX6450 / G4P) reads 0x00030a00. Accept both so the A8 driver can
bind through the t7000-gpu fallback and get as far as the ID read.

The A8 firmware loader still rejects G4G images that carry core memory,
so firmware boot of the A8X is a later step. The device tree names
apple/gfx-t7001.bin.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple.c
index a8jobs..t7001rev 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple.c
@@ -3144,6 +3144,7 @@ static int pvr_apple_s8003_prepare_job(struct pvr_apple *apple, struct pvr_job *
 
 /* The core this driver boots: CORE_REVISION major 3, minor 10 (readChipInfo 0x8479d14) */
 #define T7000_CORE_REVISION		0x00030a00
+#define T7001_CORE_REVISION		0x00070500	/* GXA6850 / G4G */
 
 /* The power manager's registers, from its base (ApplePMGR) */
 #define T7000_PMGR_PLL5			0x5004	/* the GPU's PLL: bit 30 locked */
@@ -1007,8 +1008,9 @@ static int pvr_apple_t7000_read_gpu_id(struct pvr_apple *apple, struct pvr_gpu_id *gpu_id)
 		t7000_stuck(apple, "Fender stuck after the ID read");
 		return err;
 	}
-	if (rev != T7000_CORE_REVISION) {
-		dev_err(apple_dev(apple), "CORE_REVISION %#x is not the A8's\n", rev);
+	if (rev != T7000_CORE_REVISION && rev != T7001_CORE_REVISION) {
+		dev_err(apple_dev(apple),
+			"CORE_REVISION %#x is not the A8 or A8X\n", rev);
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 	gpu_id->b = FIELD_GET(GENMASK(23, 16), rev);
-- 
